2026-11-20 22:42 Decision (ocp-infra-worker): Cilium Gateway API host-network mode. New ocp.yaml key gateway: { mode: host_network, node_selector: { LABEL: VALUE } }; default mode load_balancer = today's behaviour. OCP::Config::cilium_helm_values renders gatewayAPI.hostNetwork.enabled=true + hostNetwork.nodes.matchLabels=node_selector, plus envoy.securityContext.capabilities { keepCapNetBindService: true, envoy: [NET_ADMIN, SYS_ADMIN, NET_BIND_SERVICE] } (Cilium 1.20.0 chart: the envoy starter drops every capability unless keepCapNetBindService, so Envoy cannot bind 80/443 without it; the list repeats the chart default plus NET_BIND_SERVICE because Helm replaces lists). It travels as Cilium helm_values, which Rex::Rancher::Cilium deep-merges last over its own gatewayAPI.enabled -- no Rex::Rancher change needed; install (Bootstrap) and upgrade (OCP::Drift remedy_config -> upgrade_cilium, incl. the station walk) both carry it. Envoy then listens on 80/443 of the labelled nodes; the edge Traefik forwards to their private address. Label the gateway worker through a pool's labels: (a pool of one, e.g. gw). setup_cilium_gateway reports the labelled nodes and their InternalIP instead of expecting an LB address; setup_lb_ipam no longer reads a Gateway address in host mode.
Rejected: (1) LB-IPAM with a private IP -- Hetzner routes nothing to an address it did not assign; it needs an hcloud network route (ip -> w1) written by OCP into a network it does not own (k453: OCP creates/changes no network), and L2 announcement does not work on Hetzner. (2) NodePort -- Traefik would target 3xxxx ports that change per Service; no fixed contract. (3) Primary IP on w1 -- against the edge decision (plan §11, only r2d2 is public); stays a documented option only, not built.
Trade-offs: single node unless several are labelled (failover = label another worker, or Traefik lists several backends with health checks); Envoy binds every address of the node incl. the public one, so the k453 firewall must not allow 80/443 inbound; hostNetwork is cluster-wide in Cilium (every Gateway of the cluster, not just cilium-gateway); envoy.enabled false (embedded Envoy) is refused under host_network since the capability would then be needed on the agent; a mode switch on a running cluster takes ocp update --component cilium --force (ocp apply does not re-run the Cilium Helm release, same as cilium.devices).
k451: different code path (cert-manager release manifest args in apply_cert_manager), not touched here; on live the edge terminates public TLS and the issuer comes from OpenBao.

